From aed25ba1dff095d2ffa779c2250277a961f4332a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:54:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Keep existing disks' pacman layer before Update > Omarchy

The compatibility overlay reaches a disk before login, but the patched omarchy refresh pacman only came with runtime 4.5.0-16 through Update > Omarchy. Catch-up repaired a disk an unpatched refresh had rewritten once, at revision 71, so running the refresh again before the update broke the disk again and nothing put it back.

Catch-up now runs pacman-layer at every boot, before its revision check. The new commands step puts the image's patched omarchy-refresh-pacman and omarchy-reinstall-pkgs over Omarchy 4.5.0's, only when they are exactly the reviewed originals from the backport's digests, so a refresh before the update already keeps the layer. The repair runs at every boot too, for runtimes the commands step does not patch. A healthy disk is read and not written, a pacman.conf or mirrorlist set up some other way is left alone as before, and no package transaction runs.

Compatibility revision 73 delivers it. The runtime package is unchanged.
